## TL;DR — 60-Second Answer

**The 3 chain lengths and when to use each:**

1. **16 inches** — sits at your collarbone; works for portrait settings and turtlenecks only; most buyers regret this length
2. **18 inches** — lands just below your collarbone; flatters every neckline; this is the length to order
3. **20 inches** — drops to your upper chest; best for V-necks and layering over a shorter chain

**The single most important insight:** 18" is not the default because it's average. It's the default because a marquise pendant needs vertical negative space below the collarbone to show the stone's full length. At 16", the stone sits against your collarbone and loses the elongating effect entirely.

