## The Chain Length Illusion

The Chain Length Illusion is a predictable buyer mistake. You order 16" because that's what the model photo shows. Then you find the chain sits wrong on your actual body.

Here is what is happening. Product photography uses models with specific neck-to-chest proportions. On the model, a 16" chain falls just below the collarbone and the pendant looks elegant. On most adult women, 16" sits at or above the collarbone. In winter with a turtleneck, the stone disappears completely. In summer with a V-neck, it competes with the neckline instead of sitting cleanly below it.

A marquise pendant makes this worse than a round pendant would. The elongated shape needs vertical negative space below the collarbone to create its visual effect. At 16", the stone presses against the collarbone. There is no breathing room. The elongating flash runs into the neck instead of down the chest.

[![Marquise diamond bezel solitaire pendant showing chain fall at different lengths](/images/marquise-diamond-necklace-bezel-pendant-angle.jpg)](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-311066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

The 18" chain positions the pendant 1–1.5 inches below the collarbone on most adult bodies. That gap is exactly what a marquise pendant needs to work properly. The stone hangs in open space. The point-up flash pulls the eye down from the neck to the stone. The elongating effect is visible.

Already own a chain? Measure from your collar to the center of your chest. That tells you where an 18" chain falls on your body. If the measurement places it below your collarbone, 18" gives you the positioning you need.

The one situation where 20" makes sense as your primary chain: you're layering with a 16" collarbone chain. The 20" marquise pendant drops below the shorter chain without tangling.

## 3 Chain Lengths That Flatter a Marquise Diamond Necklace

### 16 Inches: The Collarbone Pendant

A 16" chain sits at or near the collarbone on most adult women. For a marquise pendant, this length works in two situations. First: you have a longer neck and the chain falls naturally below the collarbone. Second: you want a portrait setting — stone high on the chest, framing the face above a blazer.

The 0.25ct–0.5ct size range is the right match for 16". A smaller stone at collarbone height reads as elegant rather than delicate. A 1ct marquise at collarbone height can look heavy and formal. That limits your outfit choices.

