**Who 18" is right for:** Almost everyone. If you're buying this as a gift and you don't know the recipient's neck length, choose 18". You won't be wrong.

### 20 Inches: The Décolletage Drop

A 20" chain drops the pendant to the upper chest, into the décolletage zone. For a marquise diamond, this length has two clear use cases.

First: V-neck and open necklines. The stone sits inside the V of the neckline, framing the décolletage rather than floating above it. The marquise point aims downward into the V and the stone anchors the look. This is the most intentional and visually polished way to wear a marquise pendant with a deep neckline.

Second: layering. A 20" marquise pendant sits naturally below a 16" collarbone chain without the two chains tangling. The visual stack is clean — short chain at the collar, marquise pendant dropping below it. This works best with 0.5ct–1ct stones. The marquise should read clearly larger than the layering chain pendant.

