## Expert Summary

**By Farzana Hasan, diamond expert** | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

A marquise diamond pendant is one of the best-value fine jewelry purchases available. The elongated shape reads larger than its carat weight. A 0.5ct marquise looks like a 0.65ct round on the chest. The bezel protects both tips completely. The result is a pendant that wears every day without concern. Visual presence holds even at modest carat weights.

The most important decision is chain length. Get it wrong and the stone loses its visual effect entirely. Get it right and you have a pendant that flatters every neckline. Order 18" if you're not sure. You can adjust later but most buyers who order 18" never need to.

For value-focused buyers, the lab options at 0.5ct and 1ct are the two clearest picks in this guide. Both are [GIA](https://www.gia.edu/)- and [IGI](https://www.igi.org/)-graded — not ungraded or lower quality. You're buying a certified diamond at a price that reflects lab origin, not earth origin.

For natural-origin buyers, the 0.5ct at $2,885 is the entry point with real visual presence. The 1ct natural at $7,490 is an investment-tier gift for a milestone occasion.

**Pros:**
- Elongated shape looks larger per carat than round, oval, or cushion
- Full bezel setting provides complete tip protection — daily wear without concern
- Lab options deliver major size jumps at the same budget
- White and yellow gold identically priced at every carat weight
- Available at 3ct lab for $4,080 — a size that barely exists in affordable natural

**Cons:**
- Orientation matters — point-up vs east-west is a real decision most round-pendant buyers never have to make
- 16" chain is a common ordering mistake; most buyers need 18"
- Platinum premium adds $130–$1,115 over gold at equivalent carat weights

