## Frequently Asked Questions

### What chain length is best for a marquise diamond necklace?

18 inches is the right length for most buyers. It positions the pendant 1–1.5 inches below the collarbone. That gives the marquise stone the vertical breathing room it needs to create its elongating effect. A 16" chain lands at the collarbone for most adults and the stone loses its visual impact.

### What is the difference between point-up and east-west orientation on a marquise pendant?

Point-up means the stone's long axis runs parallel to the chain, pointing vertically downward. East-west means the stone sits horizontally across the chest. Point-up creates the classic elongating look that makes a marquise pendant different from a round. East-west is modern and architectural. Most pendant settings default to point-up.

### Is a bezel setting better than prong for a marquise diamond pendant?

Yes, for daily wear. A full bezel wraps the entire stone girdle, including both fragile pointed tips of the marquise. Prong settings leave the tips exposed and can snag fabric or gradually loosen in pendant use. A bezel pendant on a marquise is the standard professional recommendation for this shape.

### How much does a marquise diamond necklace cost?

Lab-grown marquise bezel pendants start at [$755 for 0.25ct](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-311060?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [$885 for 0.5ct](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-311062?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in 14k gold. Natural marquise pendants start at [$1,300 for 0.25ct](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-310945?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [$2,885 for 0.5ct](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-310948?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Platinum adds roughly 10–20% over gold at each carat weight.

### Does a marquise diamond necklace look bigger than a round pendant at the same carat weight?

Yes. A marquise has a larger face-up surface area than a round at the same carat weight. A 0.5ct marquise looks visually similar to a 0.65ct round on the chest. The elongated body spans more distance. It's one of the most efficient ways to get more visual presence per dollar in a diamond pendant.

### What is the best carat size for a marquise diamond pendant?

0.5ct is the sweet spot for everyday wear. It's clearly visible from conversational distance. Not heavy for daily use. The elongated shape reads larger than 0.5ct suggests. At 1ct, the pendant becomes a statement piece. Below 0.25ct, the stone can read as too delicate to see the marquise shape clearly.

### Can I wear a marquise diamond necklace every day?

Yes, in a bezel setting. The bezel protects both fragile pointed tips from impact and snagging. Diamond itself is the hardest natural substance (Mohs 10) and resists scratching in daily wear. Avoid ultrasonic cleaners at home; warm soapy water and a soft brush is enough for regular cleaning.

### Is lab-grown the same quality as natural in a marquise pendant?

Chemically, physically, and optically identical — both are 100% carbon in a diamond crystal structure. The GIA grades lab-grown marquise diamonds on the same cut, color, clarity, and carat standards as natural. The price reflects market dynamics and origin, not quality.

### Which metal is best for a marquise diamond necklace?

14k white gold is the most versatile starting choice. It works with any diamond color grade and any outfit. Yellow gold is equally priced and works especially well with H–J color stones. Platinum costs more but never needs rhodium replating. Worth considering for a pendant you wear daily for decades.

### How do I choose between a natural and lab marquise diamond pendant?

If origin, tradition, or long-term value matters to you, choose natural. If you want maximum visual size per dollar and you're buying for wear rather than investment, choose lab. Consider: [1ct lab at $1,560](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-311066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) vs [0.5ct natural at $2,885](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-310948?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). For a pendant, double the stone size for 46% less money is a compelling argument.

### What is a Toi et Moi marquise diamond necklace?

Toi et Moi means "you and me" in French. The style pairs two stones in one pendant setting. These lab pendants pair a round brilliant with a marquise diamond in a shared bezel mount. Available in [white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-316292?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), [yellow gold](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-316293?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), and [rose gold](https://www.bluenile.com/james-allen/item-316294?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at $2,535 each.

### Can a marquise diamond pendant be layered with other necklaces?

Yes. Wear a 16" chain at the collarbone and add the marquise on a 20" chain below it. The two lengths clear each other without tangling. Avoid layering two marquise pendants at the same length — they compete for the same visual space.

### What is the Chain Length Illusion?

It's the common mistake of ordering 16" because that's the length shown in product photos. You then find it sits at or above your collarbone rather than below it. Most product photography uses models whose proportions make 16" look correct. On most adult bodies, 16" touches the collarbone and the marquise stone loses its elongating effect. The fix is 18".

### What does "orient effect" mean for a marquise pendant?

It refers to the visual transformation that happens when you rotate the stone's orientation on the pendant bail. Point-up (stone pointing vertically) creates the classic elongating look. East-west (stone sitting horizontally) creates a modern, architectural look. Both are valid choices depending on your preferred style and the necklines you wear most.
